# Studio runtime state. The event log is the studio's memory of a particular
# run, not part of the tool. Delete it to reset a studio; never commit it.
.studio/

# A project's own config and brief belong to that project, not to this repo.
# They are ignored here so a clone used as its own workspace stays clean.
/studio.config.json
/PROJECT.md

# The same rule for the current layout. In someone else's project
# studio_floor/config.json is the roster and is worth committing — here it is
# just this clone dogfooding itself, and test_project/ is scratch the team
# writes while working. Untracked was not enough: a single `git add -A`, by a
# human or by an agent with a shell, would have swept both into the tool's
# own history.
/studio_floor/
/test_project/

node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

.idea/
.vscode/

# Real secrets for docker compose: the token that guards the API, the provider
# keys, the git token the team pushes with. `.env.example` is the committed
# one and carries no values.
.env
